{
  "$comment": "THE WATCHDOG (lib/sessions/watchdog.ts, trpc devices.heartbeat, sessions.report). `watchdog.tick` runs every minute; within one tick the rules run in this order, each over the sessions oldest first: (1) UNCLAIMED: queued, never started, not blocked, created more than unclaimedMinutes ago = blocked `unclaimed` + needsInput, said once (waking; with nobody listening, on itself). The claim clears it. (2) NUDGE: a running/idle session not parked `device_offline` whose host device is known and which holds pending input older than nudgeMinutes = a `nudge` of its device, once per device per tick, every tick while it lasts (no row write). (3) STUCK: running/idle, busy, not blocked, NO SIGN OF LIFE for stuckMinutes (liveness = the later of updatedAt and lastActivityAt: a report, a reply, the heartbeat's per-session activity), not listed live by its ONLINE host; a `background` run is alive for backgroundStuckMinutes first = blocked `stuck` + needsInput, said once (copy.stuck with the whole silent minutes, never fewer than the threshold). The device's next report or a heartbeat listing it clears it (needsInput re-derived from open cards). (4) OFFLINE: a busy running/idle session whose host was not seen within onlineWindowSeconds = idle, not busy, blocked `device_offline` with resume (mid-turn) and resumeSince null: an INTERRUPTION, SILENT (no line, needsInput untouched); a running one between turns on a dead host just reads idle. (5) UNRESUMED: an interruption with resume whose resumeSince is more than resumeMinutes ago and that is not yet on a person = needsInput, said once as `session_interrupted` (copy.unresumed, waking). (6) WALLS: a `rate_limit` whose RFC 3339 resetsAt has passed = cleared silently (unparseable = the device's to clear). HEARTBEAT (`device.heartbeat {liveSessionIds?, activity?}`): the device is seen now; its `device_offline` sessions: no list (an older device) or not mid-turn = cleared; listed = running + busy again; unlisted mid-turn = keeps the flag, `resumeSince` stamped now (the resume clock starts when the device is back). Activity entries (valid ids, never later than now) move lastActivityAt forward on its running/idle sessions. With a list: every running + busy session of the device NOT listed (an empty list = all of them) = idle + blocked `restarted`, resume, resumeSince now (its process died; silent); a listed `stuck` one is cleared. ANY device report clears `stuck` and the interruptions (the device is back on it); a `lost` report (process_lost / daemon_restart) never ends: idle, and mid-turn = `restarted` with resume (silent), a usage wall stays. Ids in the live list follow eCore's id rule; anything else is dropped (`liveIdCases`).",
